{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 132ca815130b0d1d230d62b0355fc22724d5b576 (tree 21347d589c68a9c209279731e574547bc29ec182), the ARC-1 B notes-only proposal on published c9038871. The verdict binds the ARC-1 B landing request's implementation promise and signs the one path artifact, notes/implementation/2026-11-22-arc1-prospective-envelope.md (f91aa05c).\n\n## What the head is\nThree notes-only commits on c9038871 change one file: the proposal (65788d98), the evidence table (2a6c5939) and the three clarifications that planner ruling 845a853d orders (132ca815). `git diff --name-only c9038871 132ca815` lists that one path. The note changes no source, test or generated module, and it proposes no change to the driver or to any pass cap.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Gate.** The notes-only gate ran on 65788d98 (tree 3c02473b). `gate.txt` (SHA-256 `fdc5abad…`) names that head and tree, shows \"changed files 0\", ends \"gate passed\" in 34.05 s, and END 20298ce0 matches. The later two commits change the same note only, so the notes-only rule applies to the head.\n- **Hashes.** All seven SHA-256 values in the note match files in `2026-11-22-65788d9-arc1-envelope-gate`: the gate and the six measurement summaries.\n- **The table.** I recomputed the per-axis maxima from the retained summaries. The Rules, Lending, Directory (15 cutoffs, all `confirmed`), Destination 15 and Destination 21 passes give entries 21, attempts 157, nodes 66, calls 551, metadata 2,603,832 and inputWork 87,072,715. Each equals the \"Largest observed\" column. The columns \"Observation to envelope\" and \"Envelope to default\" are correct arithmetic on all six rows. 3 MiB is three quarters of the 4 MiB default, and 112 MiB is seven eighths of the 128 MiB default, so the stated reserves of one quarter and one eighth are right.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main (c9038871) is clean with tree 21347d58. `git diff --check` is clean. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 3. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The added lines carry no other project's name and no private path.\n\n## The three planner edits\n1. **Name the axis.** The refusal keeps the one closed reason `archive-envelope-exceeded`, and its detail names `entries`, `attempts`, `nodes`, `calls`, `metadata` or `inputWork`, or `unbounded` when a bound is unavailable. A developer learns which part of the declaration to change.\n2. **Say what the refusal means.** A new paragraph states that the application still installs and writes normal live history, that its entries get no archive eligibility and stay under the live storage and room limits, and that they get no archive-backed export or reclamation.\n3. **Name nodes.** The note calls out nodes (66 observed, 96 proposed, 128 default) as needing an early recheck. See the non-blocking wording point.\n\n## Wake rate\nNotes only. No alarm, retry or reschedule changes, and no pass cap or driver change, so the wake floor and requests per room per hour stay as published (the planner's CJ-1 reading on dap-grow was 1,843 requests an hour, 29 a minute). The proposal bears on wakes in one direction: it limits which declarations get archive eligibility, so an ineligible entry cannot make a pass that cannot confirm and cannot hold a room at the backoff cap. It adds no schedule of its own. The note says existing entries that already exceed a future envelope stay unchanged and may still block the confirmed frontier, and that their recovery needs a separate decision.\n\n## Architecture\nThe note keeps the boundary honest. It says the thresholds are review values and not derived bounds, that the counters do not bound elapsed time, and that a sample that confirms says nothing about other accepted entries. It requires a proof that a progress unit fits one original pass before any admission check exists. It does not promise an eventual-export guarantee.\n\n## Security\nNotes only. No source, token, header or custody path changes. The refusal reason is closed and names only a counter, so a refusal leaks no user data.\n\n## Simplification\nOne envelope, one refusal reason, one detail field. Nothing to remove.\n\n## Non-blocking\n1. **Trigger wording.** Ruling 845a853d asks the note to name nodes as the first axis to recheck \"when a new covered family is measured\". The note says \"Nodes need an early recheck\" and gives the numbers, without the trigger. Add \"when a new covered family is measured\" at the next edit.\n2. **Directory evidence.** The note says Directory used an ordinary founder. The summary shows 15 confirmed cutoffs with a per-cutoff cost, and the largest (57 nodes, 253 calls) sits well under the maxima. No other Directory shape is claimed, so nothing is missing.\n3. **Order of work.** Implementation follows in the planner's order: estimator proposal, no-loss-of-eligibility check, then the admission check and refusal tests. This approval covers the note only.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f91aa05c56c047ad4f73378bf412e2ee68ee5bbf","binding":"assigned","head":"132ca815130b0d1d230d62b0355fc22724d5b576","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ad272c692f0053959988c305d2b1b25523230a54\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:082db83151555b3e1e8e3b7c0a7a3f63117b61a1\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4413e2077693494bfafd0c3acb99f0fddca6410f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eab848050ed35dc88340c10419bab1f22d6ca385","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}